# Cloudflare Tunnel token (remote-managed tunnel).
#
# How to get it:
#   1. https://one.dash.cloudflare.com  ->  Networks  ->  Tunnels
#   2. "Create a tunnel"  ->  Connector type: Cloudflared
#   3. Name it (e.g. "admiral-vps"), copy the token shown under
#      "Install and run a connector"  ->  Docker.  Only the token string
#      (the long base64 blob after `--token`) is needed here.
#   4. Under "Public Hostnames" in the same tunnel, route:
#        Subdomain:  admiral
#        Domain:     your-domain.tld
#        Service:    HTTP   ->   admiral:3031
#      (the hostname `admiral` resolves inside the compose network)
#   5. (Strongly recommended) Zero Trust  ->  Access  ->  Applications:
#      add a Self-hosted app for admiral.your-domain.tld with an email
#      allow-list. Without this, anyone with the URL can reach the UI
#      and the stored provider API keys.
CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=
